window.docContents[58].resolve({"/The-sharp-sub-Coulomb-commutator/#comm-lean-HRS___Commutator___Whole___subcoulomb_commutator_scale":{"contents":"Let  be an integer and .There is  such that, for each , there is . Let  be real with , let  be an integer and let  be pairwise distinct.When , assume .For , let  be Lipschitz withFor every ,The quantity in parentheses is nonnegative, and the mixed and background integrals defining  and  converge absolutely. Here  for ;  is uniform in , and both constants are independent of .The whole-space kernel is  for  and  for .Set . The energy and first transport commutator areThe integrals expand into the particle sum with  omitted, the mixed terms and the background term. All vector norms are Euclidean.In the transport bound,  denotes the Lipschitz seminorm. The componentwise distributional derivative  has multiplier  for the Fourier convention . Each fractional-derivative norm is the norm of a representative satisfying the distributional identity with absolutely convergent pairings against every complex Schwartz test function.\n\nVerification: Lean proof term available.\n\nSource: HRS/Commutator/Whole/Assembly.lean.\n\nDeclaration type, as written:\n\ntheorem subcoulomb_commutator_scale (hd : 3 ≤ d) {s : ℝ} (hs0 : 0 ≤ s) (hsd : s < (d : ℝ) - 2) :\n    ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ ∀ p : ℝ≥0∞, ENNReal.ofReal ((d : ℝ) / (d - s)) < p →\n      ∃ Cp : ℝ, 0 < Cp ∧ ∀ ρ : Euc d → ℝ, Integrable ρ → MemLp ρ p volume → ∫ x, ρ x = 1 →\n      (s = 0 → LogIntegrable ρ) →\n      ∀ (v : Euc d → Euc d) (K : ℝ), SubTransport d s v K →\n      ∀ (N : ℕ) (X : Fin N → Euc d), 1 ≤ N → Function.Injective X → ∀ η : ℝ, 0 < η →\n        EnergyIntegrable s X ρ ∧ CommIntegrable s X ρ v ∧\n        0 ≤ scaleQ s Cp p η X ρ ∧ |commA s X ρ v| ≤ C * K * scaleQ s Cp p η X ρ\n\n\nInspected Lean proof body:\n\nby\n  obtain ⟨C, hC, S⟩ := scale_estimate hd hs0 hsd\n  refine ⟨C, hC, fun p hp => ?_⟩\n  obtain ⟨Cp, hCp, S'⟩ := S p hp\n  refine ⟨Cp, hCp, fun ρ h1 hpρ hmass hlog v K hv N X hN hX η hη => ?_⟩\n  obtain ⟨L, hL⟩ : ∃ L : ℝ≥0, LipschitzWith L v := by\n    obtain ⟨L, F, -, hL, -, -⟩ := hv\n    exact ⟨L, hL⟩\n  obtain ⟨hE, hCI⟩ := integrable_of_Lp hd hs0 hsd p hp ρ h1 hpρ hlog v L hL X\n  obtain ⟨ρm, hbdd, hnorm, hlim⟩ := density_approx hd hs0 hsd p hp ρ h1 hpρ hmass hlog\n  obtain ⟨hF, hA⟩ := hlim N X v L hL\n  have hm := fun m => S' (ρm m) (hbdd m) N X hN hX v K hv η hη\n  have hQ : Tendsto (fun m => scaleQ s Cp p η X (ρm m)) atTop (𝓝 (scaleQ s Cp p η X ρ)) := by\n    unfold scaleQ\n    exact (hF.sub tendsto_const_nhds).add\n      (tendsto_const_nhds.mul (tendsto_const_nhds.add (hnorm.mul tendsto_const_nhds)))\n  refine ⟨hE, hCI, ge_of_tendsto hQ (Eventually.of_forall fun m => (hm m).1), ?_⟩\n  exact le_of_tendsto_of_tendsto hA.abs (tendsto_const_nhds.mul hQ)\n    (Eventually.of_forall fun m => (hm m).2)\n\n\n","context":"Fluctuations of Riesz gases\u0009The sharp sub-Coulomb commutator\u0009Lean declarations and evidence","header":"1.6.4. Whole space · arbitrary-scale theorem","id":"/The-sharp-sub-Coulomb-commutator/#comm-lean-HRS___Commutator___Whole___subcoulomb_commutator_scale"}});